{:event/id #uuid "276f2663-9855-4e52-bb7d-31bb75f685c5", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-11T23:48:19.942Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev", :lesson "Clio is the canonical ledger, and provider adapters must retain wire payload contracts while delegating schema hashes, identity, admission and causal replay to that kernel. JVM and Node interoperability tests expose durable lock guarantees that in-memory fixtures cannot cover. A frozen offline lock validation can reuse existing pinned native dependencies without re-resolving unrelated package metadata."}}
{:event/id #uuid "9c04c5df-784f-4dae-9d2a-107951d5418a", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T00:13:23.090Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev", :lesson "Current guidance and dated survey history need separate labels during a provider retirement. Reconciled Clio ownership, service payload boundaries and Rheos raw-envelope compatibility against actual manifests while retaining the August survey. Reading both package.json and bb.edn exposed divergent build targets; documentation now names the difference instead of claiming the commands are interchangeable."}}
{:event/id #uuid "14db9064-d331-4331-bb0c-1dc97db030e5", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T00:22:10.325Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev", :lesson "A ClojureScript with-redefs replacement must preserve the compiled callable shape of the real boundary, not only accept the same apparent arguments. Receipt River production git/exec-at has two arities, so callers use its arity-2 dispatch property; a single-arity delayed fixture lacked it. Reproduced before changing the fixture, retained every concurrency assertion and timer, and verified package tests, production release and lint."}}
{:event/id #uuid "c5a40627-bb89-4426-bc94-ae17ea19ba7c", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T07:25:47.418Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation", :lesson "Sol concurrent wire retry repair: p-efficiency0.9, p-friction0.2, p-skill-candidate0.3. A sequential retry test missed an unlocked planning race. Two independent handles with deterministic preemption at the real append boundary reproduced the canonical UUID/time conflict, then verified first-fact reuse and strict competing-payload refusal. Existing falsify-every-new-test and verify-the-binary lessons apply; no new spore."}}
{:event/id #uuid "ae4265a1-cbb9-468a-b02f-e1a5d5f7868f", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T07:58:14.835Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation", :lesson "Clio PR334 Node durability review: instrument the mutable CommonJS fs default and refresh built-in ESM exports before trusting fsync observations; immutable namespace patches silently observed nothing. A real baseline admitted events without schema temp/directory sync. Now schema content, atomic publication, empty ledger and ancestry are forced before acknowledgement; a partial directory failure retries existing ancestry. Friction 0.4: ptrace is unavailable in this sandbox, so evidence proves actual native-call sequencing and refusal, not physical power-loss durability. Full Clio BB25/75 JVM61/164 NBB62/151 Shadow62/151 passed with zero failures/errors, lint and compile zero warnings. No spore incubated."}}
{:event/id #uuid "85ba45fa-f575-4a04-8f73-821d2d0f5c0a", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T08:21:51.313Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation", :lesson "Warning-gate review: p-efficiency 0.85, p-friction 0.25, p-skill-candidate 0.3; no new spore. Executing the actual generated Bash and local CLI with successful processes that emit lowercase, comma-ended, bracketed Maven and positive-count warnings reproduced missed failures. Keep zero-warning and original-exit controls beside each rejection. Evidence: package-warning-gates-red/green, generated-warning-gates-red/green, warning-gates-full-cli-tests."}}
{:event/id #uuid "2d681fb4-6f19-462b-b9f4-609c23a5fddc", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T09:29:02.279Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix", :lesson "PR334 shared EDN opener: P-efficiency 0.8, P-friction 0.5, skill-candidate 0.4. Exact published source recovery worked after sandbox loss; canonical CLIs required rebuild. Sol first-open recovery did not cover the separate shared-services opener. A real two-process barrier reproduced native EEXIST, then proved winner replay and both durable writes. Full guarded protocols 71/217, strict TS, ESM111 files0warnings and kondo0/0 green. Review transition refused before broad build because unactivated shell chose runtime pnpm; card remains in_progress, with no bypass or false broad-gate claim. No new spore."}}
{:event/id #uuid "ce97e6a6-470a-4d5d-9cef-07d43972e7fc", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T09:57:30.194Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix", :lesson "PR334 review friction 3/5: a per-stream CAS cannot enforce a cross-stream Sol wire identity. Serialize the wire-ID decision and canonical append using a separate kernel-locked inode, then replay-check old histories for duplicate wire IDs. Test the actual two-process boundary and rejected inode-fsync acknowledgement, not only single-writer success. Linux retains durable EDN; unsupported Node hosts must select explicit volatile behavior instead of failing an ordinary turn."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "338b5fb3-8108-4dbe-b640-f8ff5b316bd4", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:00:20.954Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation", :lesson "Creation, append, and projection acknowledgments are distinct failure paths. Test each through real native descriptors and the public consuming provider; visibility and matching state do not prove a completed durability fence. Preserve uncertain files, validate their facts, and force inode plus parent on recovery."}}
