#:event{:id #uuid "531f993d-792d-414d-87f8-6dd4509fc818", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T14:49:44.621Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-cli"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-cli", :lesson "A public command can bypass a corrected runtime helper. Exercise the shipped launcher with an actual peer publication; subprocess completion means output pipes closed, not just leader exited. Native async metadata and quoted NODE_OPTIONS paths remain part of the fixture contract."}}
{:event/id #uuid "cd9b8881-2249-4941-aaef-92e2f1210ced", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T17:12:28.061Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-restored"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-restored", :lesson "Recovery after workspace maintenance required fresh source and tools, not trusting historical green receipts. Public exact retry must expose generated identity before a failed acknowledgment. Real CLI execution caught NBB stdout routing that source inspection missed. Peer review caught symlink/.. redirection; even Node realpathSync normalizes lexically, so verify native realpathSync.native against the actual opened target. Final current-source gates passed; hosted successor review remains separate. Friction0.65 efficiency0.8 skill-candidate0.75; existing artifact-verification and path-audit spores cover this lesson, no new spore."}}
{:event/id #uuid "6981ed92-07b1-4ca3-bf03-cbc54b543d84", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T08:25:08.131Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work", :lesson "Axxium review checkpoint a7b19825: efficiency 0.8, friction 0.35. Existing worktree recovery retained source commits but omitted later lawful card transitions; verify canonical card projection instead of trusting an earlier success message. A nonblocking cleanup finally can mask an already-committed signup, so preserve results and retain expiring leases on deferred cleanup. Account fallback safety depends on configured methods, not just stored bindings. Integrated source gates pass 66 tests/632 assertions and real TCP proof; strict legacy boundary remains 56 violations and live external consent is distinct. Existing recovery and exact-head spores cover these lessons; no new spore incubated."}}
{:event/id #uuid "23d0cdb5-148c-43f3-9105-ba636a293092", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T10:02:00.872Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work", :lesson "One-use provider exchange and local admission have different retry boundaries: keep the verified result across native lock contention, but revalidate current finite challenge and linking authority before every commit. Actual SDK/module and HTTP-header tests caught bcrypt import and cookie unit defects that adapter mocks missed. Guarded Axxium 83/744, build 119 files zero warnings, lint and unchanged strict boundary zero; live provider consent remains separately unverified. Existing review-thread and exact-head lessons cover this slice; no new spore."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "f9629cde-aa9b-43ef-838e-3f2ecea595e6", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T11:42:58.073Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity", :lesson "Recovery friction0.6, efficiency0.8, skill-candidate0.4; no new spore. Distinguish visible bytes from durable acknowledgment at every provider no-op. Real SDK callback fixtures must include the issuer DPoP key; stubbing only outer callback misses session-store failures. Preserve every historical ledger byte when merging independent append histories; fail a combined shell step before staging on script failure. Pinned source recovery plus fresh guards establishes new evidence, never transfers lost-tree results."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "9f6af1ad-e9bc-4909-b2ab-162287a89fa2", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:09:20.788Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-successor"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-successor", :lesson "A reference SDK storage test is insufficient unless the application orchestration is also exercised with distinct SDK and application state. Keep native SDK behavior real and only control the remote issuer. Pin independent consumers to immutable source copies; notifying one compiler owner does not release another consumer freeze."}}
